sequenceDiagram
    participant "Backend API Host" as BackendAPIHost
    participant "AWS CloudWatch" as AWSCloudWatch
    participant "Amazon SNS" as AmazonSNS

    activate BackendAPIHost
    BackendAPIHost->>BackendAPIHost: 1. Serves continuous production traffic (e.g., GET /api/v1/dashboard).
    BackendAPIHost-->>BackendAPIHost: HTTP 200 OK with dashboard data
    BackendAPIHost->>AWSCloudWatch: 2. [OTLP Exporter] Publishes performance metric for each completed request.
    AWSCloudWatch->>AWSCloudWatch: 3. [Alarm Evaluation] Continuously evaluates 'ApiLatencyP95Alarm' every minute.
    AWSCloudWatch-->>AWSCloudWatch: Evaluation Result: OK or BREACHING
    AWSCloudWatch->>AWSCloudWatch: 4. [State Change] Transitions 'ApiLatencyP95Alarm' state to 'ALARM' after sustained threshold breach.
    AWSCloudWatch-->>AWSCloudWatch: New State: ALARM
    activate AmazonSNS
    AWSCloudWatch->>AmazonSNS: 5. [Alarm Action] Publishes alert message to SNS Topic 'OnCall-Alerts-Topic'.
    AmazonSNS->>AmazonSNS: 6. [Fan-out] Delivers notification message to all configured topic subscribers.

    note over BackendAPIHost: Scenario Trigger: A slow database query is introduced in a new deployment, causing the '/api/v1/d...
    note over AWSCloudWatch: All monitoring infrastructure (Metric Filters, Alarms, SNS Topic, Subscriptions) is defined as co...
    note over AWSCloudWatch: The CloudWatch Alarm state change is a security-auditable event, automatically logged to AWS Clou...

    deactivate AmazonSNS
    deactivate BackendAPIHost
